          "message": {
            "text": "The E2E lane now uses the production persistent native-helper transport while owning its Vitest-fork lifecycle explicitly. Native Linux x64 keeps the retained 192-cell counter fixture below its restored 60-second deadline at 28.298 seconds and the complete headless pool exits cleanly. A prior native one-shot run was also sub-60, so the original overrun is attributed to qemu-emulated x64 timing and persistence is not claimed as the dominant speedup; the attached profile records that distinction and the residual capture/text costs.",
            "markdown": "The E2E lane now uses the production persistent native-helper transport while owning its Vitest-fork lifecycle explicitly. Native Linux x64 keeps the retained 192-cell counter fixture below its restored 60-second deadline at 28.298 seconds and the complete headless pool exits cleanly. A prior native one-shot run was also sub-60, so the original overrun is attributed to qemu-emulated x64 timing and persistence is not claimed as the dominant speedup; the attached profile records that distinction and the residual capture/text costs."
          },
